-- title:
--   Strong approximation for Eichler orders away from a split place
-- statement:
--   Let $a,b\in\mathbb Q$ and let $q'$ be a prime with $q'\ge 5$ such that `IsDefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt a b q'` holds, i.e. $a<0$, $b<0$, and for every height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal O_{\mathbb Q}$ the completed algebra $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb Q_v$ has all its nonzero elements invertible exactly when $q'\in v$. Let $N$ be a nonzero natural number and let $R$ be a $\mathbb Z$-submodule of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]$ which is an Eichler order of level $N$, that is, $R=\Lambda_1\cap\Lambda_2$ for two maximal orders $\Lambda_1,\Lambda_2$ (orders maximal for inclusion among orders) with the relative index of $R$ in $\Lambda_1$, as additive subgroups, equal to $N$; no squarefreeness of $N$ is assumed. Let $r$ be a prime with $r\ne q'$, let $v$ be a height-one prime of $\mathcal O_{\mathbb Q}$ with $r\in v$, and let $x$ be a unit of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb A_{\mathbb Q}^{f}$, where $\mathbb A_{\mathbb Q}^{f}$ is the finite adele ring of $\mathbb Q$. Then there exist $\gamma\in\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]^\times$ and units $g,u$ of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb A_{\mathbb Q}^{f}$ such that $u$ stabilises, under multiplication, the additive subgroup generated by the elements $z\otimes a$ with $z\in R$ and $a$ an adele that is integral at every place; the image of $g$ under the evaluation map $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb A_{\mathbb Q}^{f}\to\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb Q_w$ is $1$ for every height-one prime $w\ne v$; and $x$ equals the product of the diagonal image of $\gamma$, then $g$, then $u$. The hypothesis $r\ne q'$ is used through the place $v$ being a place where the algebra splits, and $r$ is allowed to divide $N$.
--
--   This is strong approximation (Eichler, Kneser) for the unit group of a definite quaternion algebra over $\mathbb Q$, relative to an Eichler order $R$ of arbitrary level $N$, in double-coset form: $\widehat{\mathbb H}^\times=\mathbb H^\times\cdot\mathbb H_v^\times\cdot\widehat R^\times$ for a finite place $v$ at which $\mathbb H$ is split, so that every class in $\mathbb H^\times\backslash\widehat{\mathbb H}^\times/\widehat R^\times$ has a representative supported at $v$. It is the surjectivity input for the comparison of the vertex and edge quotients of the Čerednik–Drinfeld coset graph with the class set of an Eichler order.
